# Publish a Content Entity, update it in a later Batch, read it as a User.
# Deleted ids are never reused, so bump @run before running the file again.
@run = 1
@id = happy-{{run}}

### Publish v1
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "Hello" } }
]

### Read it (wait ~1s for the worker): version 1
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}

### Publish v2
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 2, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T11:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "Hello again" } }
]

### Read it: version 2, updatedAt 11:00
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}

### List: newest first
GET {{host}}/entities?limit=10
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}
